# emtrc plan v2: from websites to an AI-run services company

Nov 21, 2026 · @Kieran Pascal

## Summary

emtrc becomes an AI-run services company for London small businesses. Websites are the way in; recurring AI, comms and security services are the business. Claude (Cowork, Code and the API) does most of the delivery and admin, and you approve anything that reaches a person or moves money. Stage 1 is still the [v1 plan](https://claude.ai/artifact/VD6b5MfgGcm9g6ks7e7CBs): 10 website clients by about February 2027 on £50, then £100. v2 covers what comes after, and supersedes v1 where they differ.

**What changed from v1:**

- **Domains move to Cloudflare Registrar.** It sells at cost, your DNS and Pages are already there, and it now handles .uk. Porkbun is the fallback for extensions Cloudflare doesn't sell.
- **The first upsell is the review engine (£39/mo), not the full Lead Catcher.** It's the easiest yes, and it opens the door to the rest of the ladder.
- **Postcards with a QR code to each business's own demo become the scalable channel for sole traders.** Post is outside PECR, and the Stannp API automates it.
- **New free lead feeds catch businesses the week they open:** food hygiene registrations, new Companies House incorporations and council licence lists.
- **The PSTN switch-off on 31 January 2027 is confirmed.** About 1.2 million lines are still on copper, so phones become a stage-2 product, not a stage-3 one.
- **Claude plans were renamed on about 1 November 2026.** Max is $100/mo (5x Pro), Ultra is $200/mo. Buy Max in January and move up only if you keep hitting the weekly limit.
- **Cowork now runs in the cloud by default,** so scheduled jobs run with your PC off. Local folders and browser use still need the desktop app open.

