## VoIP, IT and other bolt-ons

**Add only low-touch services, ranked by margin multiplied by how little work they take. Never do on-site break-fix, WiFi installs, handset installs or self-hosted phone servers.** \[V\] = live page read.

### The phone opportunity: PSTN switch-off

The 31 January 2027 deadline is confirmed and unchanged ([ISPreview, Sep 2026](https://ispreview.co.uk/index.php/2026/09/openreach-confirm-post-january-2027-measures-for-uk-analogue-phone-switch-off.html)) \[V\]. About 1.2 million lines are still on copper, including about 350,000 business premises. Lines not migrated go onto "Emergency Voice Access", which providers pay £35/mo wholesale for from 1 February 2027, and orders completing after 31 March 2027 are cancelled.

- **Until January:** "Get off copper before you're moved onto an emergency line."
- **From February, all of 2027:** "You were moved onto a basic digital line. Upgrade to a cloud phone with an AI receptionist."
- **Refer out, don't touch:** alarm lines, card terminals, lift and telecare lines.

