## Lead generation by stage

**Catch businesses in the week they open, reach sole traders by post and in person, and let Claude run the whole pipeline while you do the human contact.** Scraping more gives diminishing returns. Timing and personalisation drive conversion.

### Free intent feeds

| Signal | Source | What it finds | Use |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| New food businesses | [FSA Food Hygiene Rating API](https://www.food.gov.uk/food-hygiene-rating-scheme-api-version-2) (free, no key) | Places marked "Awaiting Inspection" = newly registered cafés, takeaways, home bakers | Weekly pull per London borough |
| New limited companies | [Companies House Streaming API](https://developer-specs.company-information.service.gov.uk/streaming-api/guides/overview) (free key) | Real-time new incorporations; filter SIC 96020, 43210, 56101, 81210 + London postcodes | Match to Maps for contact details. These can be emailed |
| New premises licences | Council registers, e.g. [Royal Greenwich weekly list](https://www.royalgreenwich.gov.uk/licensingapplications), Tower Hamlets, City, Richmond, Wandsworth, Merton | Bars, takeaways, late-night venues before opening | Weekly scrape per borough |
| Special treatment licences | Borough registers (nails, massage, tattoo, sunbeds; London-specific law) | New salons before they open | Check each borough |
| New Google listings | Monthly Places API re-run, compare place IDs | Fewer than 10 reviews + no website = new business | Built into the pipeline |
| Hiring | Indeed, Reed | Growing businesses with cash | Scoring bonus only |

**Lead score (automated):** opened in last 90 days +30, no website +25, social-only +15, bad site +15, 10+ reviews at 4.3 stars or better +10, Ltd company +10 (can be emailed), tier-1 niche +10, on TPS −10 (post or walk-in only). Skip Ordnance Survey AddressBase: it's paid and has no business names.

