## Sales: offers, guarantees, upsells, retention

**Keep the v1 tiers (Starter £99 + £39, Business £199 + £69, Growth £399 + £129). Add two entry offers and three guarantees, and run a fixed upsell calendar.** The 12-month term with Direct Debit, not the setup fee, is the real value.

**New entry offers:**

| Offer | Price | For |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Claim your demo (site already built) | £0 setup on a 12-month Business term, or £99 on Starter | Demo-first leads from stage 2 (keep the £99 founding price for the first 10) |
| Launch Pack: site + Google profile + logo + domain + 1 mailbox | £299 setup + £69/mo | Just-opened leads (food hygiene, licences, new companies) |
| White-label site + hosting + care for agencies | £25 to £40/site/mo wholesale + £99 to £199 build | Stage 4, under a separate brand |

**Guarantees:**

1. **See it before you pay.** The demo already exists.
2. **30-day love it or leave it.** Cancel within 30 days of launch and get the setup fee back.
3. **Leads or a free month.** No calls or form enquiries in the first 90 days means next month is free. It's low risk with tracked forms and click-to-call.
4. **You own your domain, always,** against Yell's lock-in.

**Working conversion targets (to measure, not sourced):**

| Step | Walk-in | Call | Postcard | Ltd email |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Sees demo | 90% | 40% | 3 to 6% scan | 10 to 20% click |
| Interested | 20 to 30% | 10 to 15% | 30% of scanners | 15% of clickers |
| Closes | 8 to 12% of demos | 3 to 6% | 1 to 2% of cards | 1 to 3% |

**45-second walk-in script:** "Hi, is the owner around? I'm \[name\] from emtrc, a local web studio. \[Business\] doesn't have a website yet, so we built you one. Can I show you? It takes 20 seconds." Show the phone. "It has your reviews, prices and a WhatsApp button. It can be live this week, £69 a month including your domain and email. Can I WhatsApp you the link?" Getting a yes is your consent to follow up; log it in the CRM.

**Pricing psychology:** three tiers with the middle highlighted; charm prices (£69); show the daily equivalent ("about £2.27 a day"); anchor against Checkatrade (£100+/mo) and a £1,500 to £3,000 agency build; annual prepay gets 2 months free, pushed at signup and at month 3. Target 25 to 35% of clients on annual by stage 2.

**Upsell calendar:**

| When | What |
| --- | --- |
| Day 0 | Business over Starter (domain + email included); review engine + chat |
| Day 30 | Results report + review ask; missed-call text-back; booking or ordering |
| Day 90 | Google profile management + AI visibility; AI receptionist for trades and busy salons |
| Months 6 to 9 | Annual prepay; Growth tier; phones (PSTN angle) |
| Month 11 | Renewal call with the year's results and a new feature: the key churn moment |

**Retention:** Direct Debit (almost no failed-payment churn), annual prepay, the monthly value email, a £10/mo "pause" for seasonal businesses, a downgrade path to Starter instead of cancelling, outreach when traffic drops, and an exit survey. Most churn will be businesses closing, which you can't prevent. Quarterly one-question NPS: promoters get asked for a referral (one free month per referred client). Targets: churn under 2.5%/mo by stage 2, under 1.5% by stage 3.

