### People and scale levers

- **First VA (stage 2, once recurring revenue passes £1,200/mo):** a Philippines VA via OnlineJobs.ph, 20 hrs/week, about $400 to $600/mo, on a contractor agreement with data-processing and NDA terms. Claude writes the SOPs.
- **Commission-only reps (stage 3):** £150 per Business close + 10% of their clients' monthly fees for 12 months, 90-day clawback. They must be genuinely self-employed, or they may be owed minimum wage; re-check the Employment Rights Act 2025 status changes before hiring. You are jointly liable for unlawful calls they make for you.
- **Buying client books (stage 4):** small deals sell at a median 2.0× seller's earnings ([webhosting.today, Sep 2026](https://webhosting.today/2026/09/09/what-is-your-hosting-business-worth-the-smallest-deals-are-back-at-2-0x/)) \[V\]. Pay at most 1× annual recurring revenue, with 40%+ contingent on 12-month retention. Best deals are off-market: retiring London freelancers with 20 to 100 hosting clients. Live comparison: [Acquire.com listing, 38 clients, $122k/yr](https://app.acquire.com/public/146l8fwchy-subscription-website-design-management-service-122k-arr-38-active-clients-76-margins) \[S\]. Check domain ownership, Direct Debit transferability, contract assignment and GDPR before buying.
- **Beyond London (stage 4):** Birmingham (42% of listings have no website), Manchester, Leeds, Bristol, Glasgow. The pipeline is national; replace walk-ins with postcards, calls and local reps.
- **No franchising:** £10k to £30k of legal setup for a low-ticket product. White label gives the same leverage.

